cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "JVP Trilogy: the cybernetic limits of conversion, CBRA data requirements, and five ways an EEG geometry method looked validated"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Perazzolo
    given-names: "João Vitor"
abstract: >-
  Three interlinked papers and a pre-registered in-silico validation suite.
  The software component provides SPD/density-matrix manifold geometry
  (square-root, affine-invariant, log-Euclidean and Bures-Wasserstein metrics),
  jump-diffusion simulation with Cartan anti-development, Helmholtz-Hodge
  decomposition, and geodesic change-point detectors for non-stationary
  multichannel signals on curved state spaces. Every experimental claim is
  backed by a pre-registration written before execution and a committed raw
  result.json; see METHODOLOGY.md.
keywords:
  - Riemannian geometry
  - SPD manifolds
  - change-point detection
  - jump-diffusion
  - EEG
  - non-stationary time series
  - pre-registration
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fcadusims-droid/ACADEMIC-JVP-WORK-"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-28"
